      "writtenOn": "2020-08-21T20:05:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve puzzled through this and determined we\u0027re OK for cases with well-behaved port partners.\n\nSo multi-stage AMS initiated locally starting as Source:\n- Source sets NG first time, all subsequent AMS messages get to fall through, regardless of new power role (previously only checked when source power role) \n\nStarting as Sink:\n- Sink waits for OK first message, subsequent messages should still have OK unless port partner is misbehaving\n\nFor non-locally initiated AMSes, we skip all this logic since pe_in_local_ams() returns false.",
